{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"# Task: Review Register VM → WebAssembly Lowering Plan\n# Role: architect\n# Model: gemini-4-argon\n# Invocation: `-m gemini-4-argon --mode plan --sandbox`\n# Prompt: collab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.prompt.md\n# Date: 2026-10-18\n\n## Overview\n\nIndependent second-architect review of [`collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md), audited against the implementation and design specifications in [`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc), [`src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc), [`docs/design/datom.world.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/datom.world.md), [`docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md), [`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md), [`docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md), [`docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md), [`test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc), and [`test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc).\n\nThe plan's core architectural choices — i32 `ValueRef` handles into a task-owned arena (§1.1), body-indexed wasm functions driven by an explicit host trampoline with zero guest continuation state on the native wasm stack (§2.1), exact `r2` (descriptor version 4) 23-opcode lowering without inventing a new guest register namespace (§2.3), and staged append-only `attach-image` table growth (§5) — are sound and respect the repository's six foundational invariants. However, several concrete semantic and engine-seam discrepancies exist between the plan's specified transitions and the implementation in `register.cljc`, `debruijn_register_effects.cljc`, and `engine.cljc` that would cause differential test failures or heap-GC corruption if implemented as written.\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Audit by Review Area\n\n### 1. Semantic Fidelity (`register.cljc`, `debruijn_register_code.cljc`, `debruijn_register_effects.cljc`)\n\n1. **`register-restore` with `:resume-mode :return-result` on empty `:continuation` omits `:pc (:pc entry)` (`MAJOR`)**:\n   - In [`register.cljc:461-468`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L461-L468), `write-back` restores `:pc (:pc entry)` onto `base` *before* calling `return-transition`:\n     ```clojure\n     (if (= :return-result (:resume-mode entry))\n       (return-transition (assoc base\n                                 :pc (:pc entry)\n                                 :frames (:frames entry)\n                                 :continuation (:continuation entry)\n                                 :store-of (:store-of entry)\n                                 :halted? false)\n                          val)\n       ...)\n     ```\n   - When `(:continuation entry)` is non-empty, `return-transition` ([`register.cljc:433-454`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L433-L454)) overwrites `:pc` with `(:return-pc frame)`. When `(:continuation entry)` is empty (`[]`, e.g., a tail-call effect in body 0 or a tail call reached via tail calls from body 0), `return-transition` ([`register.cljc:432`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L432)) returns `(assoc vm :halted? true, :value val, :store-of nil)` without touching `:pc` or `:registers`. Consequently, on empty `K`, the halted VM's `:pc` is `(:pc entry)` (`(inc site-pc)`) and its `:registers` remains `(:registers base)`.\n   - Plan §3.2 step 5 ([`findings.md:147`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L147)) states: *\"For return-result restore captured K/frames/store-of then run the ordinary return transition.\"* Omitting `:pc (:pc entry)` leaves `:pc` at `(:pc base)` when `K` is empty, breaking `IVMState/control` (`{:pc (:pc vm)}`) and raw `:pc` parity in W2/W3.\n\n2. **Bidirectional synchronization between the Clojure VM record map keys and the wasm linear-memory header/shadow (`MAJOR`)**:\n   - Plan §1.2 ([`findings.md:37-46`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L37-L46)) and §4.1 ([`findings.md:163-168`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L163-L168)) place active execution fields (`pc`, active registers, `frames`, `continuation`, `store-of`, `value`, `halted`, `blocked`) in linear memory and expose `read-state(state)`.\n   - In [`engine.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc) and [`register_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc), the VM state is manipulated as a persistent Clojure record/map directly — not exclusively through `IVM`/`IVMState` methods:\n     - `engine/collect` ([`engine.cljc:2541-2603`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2541-L2603)), triggered automatically inside `engine/handle-effect` on `:cell/new` ([`engine.cljc:2605-2614, 2720`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2605-L2614)), calls `module/gc-roots` ([`register.cljc:944-949`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L944-L949)), which reads `[(:continuation vm)]` and `[(:registers vm) (:frames vm)]` directly from the `vm` map. If `:continuation`, `:registers`, and `:frames` are not materialized onto the Clojure `vm` map before `engine/handle-effect` runs, `engine/collect` will trace stale or empty roots and sweep live heap cells.\n     - `engine/handle-effect` ([`engine.cljc:2746`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2746)) sets `:value (:value result)` on `result-state` for every effect (including non-blocking `:store-put`, `:stream-make`, `:stream-cursor`, `:stream-close`, `:cell/*`, and immediate `:stream-put`/`:stream-next`), and `register.cljc:558-561, 577-580` preserves that `:value` on the VM map. If the wasm adapter overwrites `:value` on the Clojure map from its pre-effect linear-memory `value` slot upon returning from a non-blocking `HOST_SERVICE`, `(:value vm)` / `(vm/value vm)` after a non-blocking effect step will be stale (nil instead of the effect result).\n     - Callers and tests directly read `(:registers vm)` ([`register_test.cljc:292-294, 491`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc#L292-L294)), `(:pc vm')` ([`register_test.cljc:490`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc#L490)), and mutate the VM map via `(assoc parked :pc 2 :halted? false)` before calling `(vm/run vm-resumer)` ([`register_test.cljc:444-445`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc#L444-L445)).\n   - The plan must require that: (a) the Clojure VM record keys (`:pc`, `:registers`, `:frames`, `:continuation`, `:store-of`, `:value`, `:halted?`, `:blocked?`) are materialized on the state map before every `engine/*` call and at every public return (`step`, `run`, `restore`), and (b) wasm entry (`step`/`run`) synchronizes from those Clojure map keys whenever they diverge from the cached linear-memory state header/shadow.\n\n3. **`:call` of `:host-fn` returning a `module/effect?` omits blocking and `:park-entry-fns` contract (`MAJOR`)**:\n   - Plan §2.3 ([`findings.md:95`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L95)) says: *\"Host fn: apply registered implementation, check typed effect authorization, route effect through engine; ordinary result writes rd/next or executes return transition for tail.\"*\n   - In [`register.cljc:533-545, 564-580, 709-719`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L533-L580), `run-call-effect` builds `payload = (payload-of vm inst)` at the `:call` site (`site-pc = pc`, `pc = (inc pc)`, `:resume-mode` = `:return-result` if `tail?` else `:write-result`, `:dest` = `nil` if `tail?` else `rd`), passes `{:park-entry-fns (park-entry-fns payload)}` (covering `:stream/put`, `:stream/next`, and `:module/require` — which [`module.cljc:581-584`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L581-L584) also uses as fallback for `:module/try-require`) to `engine/handle-effect`, and then:\n     - When `blocked?` is `true`, returns `(assoc state :pc (inc pc))` (advancing `:pc` to `pc + 1` on the blocked VM state without writing `rd` or running `return-transition`).\n     - When `blocked?` is `false` and `tail?` is `true`, runs `(return-transition state value)` on the post-effect `state` (preserving state changes such as `:store`, `:module-stores`, `:resources`, `:heap`, `:gc`, `:id-counter`).\n     - When `blocked?` is `false` and `tail?` is `false`, returns `(assoc state :pc (inc pc) :registers (assoc (:registers state) rd value))`.\n\n4. **`:halt` and empty-`K` `:return` must preserve `:pc`, `:registers`, and `:frames` on the halted VM (`MINOR`)**:\n   - In [`register.cljc:432, 745-747`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L745-L747), `:halt` and empty-`K` `:return` set `:halted? true, :value val, :store-of nil` and leave `:pc` at the `:halt`/`:return` instruction pc (not `pc + 1`), while retaining the halting body's `:registers` and `:frames` (asserted directly in [`register_test.cljc:292-295`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc#L292-L295)). Plan §2.3 ([`findings.md:98-99`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L98-L99)) should explicitly state that `:pc`, `:registers`, and `:frames` are preserved unchanged on `:halt` and final `:return`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Continuation Correctness\n\n- **Multi-shot `:current-continuation`, tail-call `K`, and abortive invocation**:\n  - Because every guest `:call` saves an immutable sparse return frame in `K` and returns `TRANSFER` to the host trampoline before the callee body runs (§2.1, [`findings.md:70-71`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L70-L71)), the native wasm stack has depth 1 during body execution and depth 0 at every trampoline boundary.\n  - Multi-shot `:current-continuation` works without native stack copying because `:frames`, `:regs`, and `:continuation` in the captured payload are immutable records; invoking a reified continuation multiple times via `:call` (`:continuation` arm, [`register.cljc:729-733`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L729-L733)) abortively replaces `:pc`, `:frames`, `:registers`, `:continuation`, and `:store-of` from the capture without mutating the captured payload.\n  - Note on `:call` of `:continuation` ([`findings.md:95, 151`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L95)): In [`register.cljc:676, 729-733`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L676), ownership is checked inside `engine/operator-kind` ([`engine.cljc:691-708`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L691-L708)) *before* `engine/continuation-argument` validates the 1-arg arity (`:continuation-arity`). The plan should preserve that exact check order (`engine/operator-kind` before `engine/continuation-argument`) so an unowned continuation called with wrong arity raises `:foreign-continuation`, not `:continuation-arity`.\n- **Linker §7.3 r6 image membership vs layout equivalence**:\n  - Correctly analyzed in §3.2 ([`findings.md:142`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L142)), §3.3 ([`findings.md:157`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L157)), and §7 item 2 ([`findings.md:258`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L258)).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Invariant Audit (`docs/design/datom.world.md`)\n\n- **No hidden global state**: Satisfied. Value arenas and linear memories are task-owned and explicitly passed (§1.1–1.2); `id-counter` is the task's counter; module registries and primitive tables remain values in VM state.\n- **No implicit control flow / no callbacks**: Satisfied. No JS Promises, Asyncify, or browser event callbacks resume a retained wasm activation (§2.1, §4.1). Blocking returns `BLOCKED` to the scheduler.\n- **No shared mutable state**: Satisfied in principle (§1.2–1.3, §7 item 4), subject to fixing the bidirectional Clojure-map/linear-memory synchronization noted in Finding 2 above so stepping or mutating an old VM snapshot never aliases another snapshot's active register shadow.\n- **No layer collapsing**: Satisfied. Interpretation/admission (`register-image-defect`, `body-liveness`, `A → R` derivation) remains separate from wasm code generation and execution.\n- **No assumed graphs**: Satisfied. CFG construction uses validated instruction tuples and explicit body bounds (§2.2).\n- **Unitarity (A is the only code identity; AST retrievability)**: Satisfied. Wasm binaries have no code identity, are never published to `dao.jing` or indexed as a format identity, and are cached only as disposable local execution artifacts keyed by `(A, R, abi-version, features)` (§Decision, §5, §7 item 9).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Blocking, Effects, and FFI (`engine.cljc`, `ffi.cljc`, `yin.vm.engine.md`)\n\n1. **`effects/wait-entry-defect` does not accept `:module/require` / `:module/try-require` wait entries (`MINOR`)**:\n   - Plan §4.2 ([`findings.md:175`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L175)) states: *\"`effects/wait-entry-defect` is an acceptance oracle for newly built waits.\"*\n   - In [`debruijn_register_effects.cljc:372-379`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc#L372-L379), `wait-entry-defect` only recognizes `:ffi-writer`, `:ffi-reader`, `:stream-writer` (`:reason :put`), and `:stream-reader` (`:reason :next`), and rejects any other wait entry with `{:rule :wait-shape}`.\n   - However, `:module/require` and `:module/try-require` ([`module.cljc:601-636`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L601-L636)) enqueue wait entries with `:reason :link-request`, `:reason :link-response`, and `:reason :install` (and under custody gate `:running`, `:stream/poll` enqueues `:reason :observe` at [`engine.cljc:2706`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2706)). Using `effects/wait-entry-defect` as an unconditional oracle on all wait-set entries will fail on module-link waits in W4 and gated `:observe` waits in W3. Scope the `effects/wait-entry-defect` assertion in the test harness to stream (`:put`/`:next`) and FFI (`:call-id`/`:request-sent`) wait entries, and use `effects/continuation-defect` plus link-wait shape assertions for `:link-request`/`:link-response`/`:install`.\n\n2. **Custody gates (`:yin.k/gate` / `vm/gate-mode`) across stream effects, FFI, and wait-set polling (`MINOR`)**:\n   - Plan §2.3 mentions custody gates only for `:resume` ([`findings.md:111`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L111)).\n   - In [`engine.cljc:2162-2189, 2664-2715`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2162-L2189), [`ffi.cljc:209-218`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc#L209-L218), and [`module.cljc:541, 614-636`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L614-L636), `:yin.k/gate` (`:running`, `:exporting`, `:ended`) governs:\n     - `ffi/put-request` (parks in `:request-sent` without appending to `call-in` under any gate),\n     - `engine/check-wait-set` (suppresses FFI response polling, link polling, and stream `:put`/`:next` polling under any gate; steps install children only in `:running`),\n     - `:stream/cursor` (unminted cursor in `:running`; refused in `:exporting`/`:ended`),\n     - `:stream/put` (attaches `:yin.k/issue` on full in `:running`),\n     - `:stream/poll` (parks with `:reason :observe, :op :poll` on blocked in `:running`),\n     - `:stream/close` (refused under any gate), and\n     - `:module/require` / `:module/try-require` (parks in `:link-request` without minting a cursor or appending).\n   - Explicitly list `:yin.k/gate` (and `:yin.k/next-issue`) among preserved engine state roots in §1.2 and add custody-gate parity cases to W3.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Module Growth (`register.cljc`, `linker.cljc`, `yin.vm.linker.md`)\n\n- **Component-relative wasm codegen vs combined `:segment` absolute pcs (`MINOR`)**:\n  - Plan §5 step 3 ([`findings.md:194`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L194)) recommends compiling each component image with component-relative constants plus an instance `base` offset so cached `WebAssembly.Module` artifacts can be reused across tasks with different attachment orders.\n  - To keep this consistent with §2.2, §2.3, and §3.1:\n    1. Every pc written into the Task Header (`pc` on exit, `site-pc` and `return-pc` in return frames, and `:body-pc` in minted `:closure` records) must have the instance `base` offset added by the wasm instance before returning to the host.\n    2. When the host constructs a continuation payload via `effects/continuation-payload` ([`debruijn_register_effects.cljc:84-120`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc#L84-L120)), it must fetch `inst` from the relocated combined `(:segment vm)` at the absolute `(:pc vm)` — never from the unrelocated component image — because `continuation-defect` validates `(:live payload)` against `(nth (:instructions (:segment payload)) (:site-pc payload))` in the combined segment.\n- **`attach-image` on an empty base VM**:\n  - When a VM is created with `nil` or empty image (`{:bodies [] :instructions []}`), `install-image` ([`register.cljc:139`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L139)) initializes `:images` to `[[empty-R 0 0]]`, `:registers []`, and `:halted? true`. When `attach-image` ([`register.cljc:192-227`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L192-L227)) attaches a non-empty image to that empty base, `offset` is `0`, `:images` becomes `[[empty-R 0 0] [R 0 len]]` (length 2, so `:images` is included in continuation payloads!), and `:registers` and `:halted?` remain `[]` and `true` until `reset` or closure entry. W4 ([`findings.md:239`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L239)) mentions `empty-base row`; §5 should state explicitly that `create-vm` with an empty image seeds `[empty-R 0 0]` and that `attach-image` does not unhalt or resize `:registers` on the active state.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Slices and Acceptance (`corpus.cljc`, `register_test.cljc`)\n\n- The W0–W6 slice progression is well-ordered, falsifiable, and properly grounds both [`test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc) (which contains open ASTs with free variables `f`, `g`, `h`, `k`, `x`, `y`, `c`, `loop`, `s` and unparked `:p`, `:p1`, `:q` targets) and [`test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc).\n- No silent behavior-narrowing was found in W0–W5; unsupported canonical-semantic fragment cases and linker continuation-slice exports are explicitly tested for their exact qualified refusals.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Design Contradictions Verified Against Code\n\nAll three implementation-vs-design-doc discrepancies identified in the plan ([`findings.md:15-17`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L15-L17)) were independently verified against the codebase and confirmed accurate:\n1. **Return frames do not carry `:segment` or `:hash`, and restore never overwrites code space**: [`docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:864-878`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md#L864-L878) still shows `{:segment ... :hash <R> ...}` on return frames, whereas [`register.cljc:694-701`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L694-L701) and [`debruijn_register_effects.cljc:155-210`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc#L155-L210) implement [`docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md` §7.3 r6/r7](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md#L1538-L1543): return frames carry `{:site-pc :return-pc :frames :regs :live :dest}` + optional `:store-of`, and `write-back` ([`register.cljc:457-487`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L457-L487)) never overwrites `:segment`, `:hash`, or `:images`.\n2. **`:resource-updates`, not `:store-updates`**: [`docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:911, 953`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md#L911) and [`docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:82, 134, 152`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md#L82) still say `:store-updates`, whereas [`engine.cljc:2301-2310`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2301-L2310), [`ffi.cljc:292`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc#L292), and [`debruijn_register_effects.cljc:360`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc#L360) use `:resource-updates` merged into private `:resources` (per linker §7.3 r8/r9).\n3. **`vm/machine-data?` vs `plain-data?` and `engine/encoder` continuation refusal**: Confirmed in [`vm.cljc:1592-1607`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc#L1592-L1607) and [`engine.cljc:980-991`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L980-L991).\n\n---\n\n## Verdict\n\nAPPROVE WITH CHANGES\n\n- `MAJOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:147` | Semantic fidelity (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:431-432, 461-468`): In `write-back`, `:resume-mode :return-result` sets `:pc (:pc entry)` on `base` before calling `return-transition`. When `(:continuation entry)` is empty (`[]`), `return-transition` halts without modifying `:pc` or `:registers`, so the halted VM's `:pc` is `(:pc entry)` (`(inc site-pc)`), not `(:pc base)`. Plan §3.2 step 5 omits `:pc (:pc entry)` on the `return-result` branch. | Update §3.2 step 5 so `return-result` restores `:pc (:pc entry)`, `:frames (:frames entry)`, `:continuation (:continuation entry)`, `:store-of (:store-of entry)`, and `:halted? false` on `base` (while leaving `:registers` as `(:registers base)`) before running `return-transition`.\n- `MAJOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:37-46, 163-168` | Engine seam & state representation (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:44-70, 944-949`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2541-2614, 2720, 2746`, `test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc:292-295, 444, 490-491`): `engine.cljc` and existing tests read and `assoc` Clojure map keys (`:pc`, `:registers`, `:frames`, `:continuation`, `:store-of`, `:value`, `:halted?`, `:blocked?`) directly on the VM record without calling `read-state`. Specifically, `engine/handle-effect` on `:cell/new` triggers `engine/collect` -> `module/gc-roots`, which reads `(:continuation vm)`, `(:registers vm)`, and `(:frames vm)` directly from the map; `engine/handle-effect` also sets `:value` on `result-state` for non-blocking effects; and `register_test.cljc:444` mutates `(assoc parked :pc 2 :halted? false)` before `vm/run`. | Require in §1.2 and §4.1 that: (1) every exit from wasm to a host service or public return materializes `:pc`, `:registers`, `:frames`, `:continuation`, `:store-of`, `:value`, `:halted?`, and `:blocked?` onto the Clojure VM map before `engine/*` runs, (2) non-blocking host services preserve the `:value` set by `engine/handle-effect` rather than clobbering it from the pre-call wasm header, and (3) wasm entry (`step`/`run`) synchronizes from the Clojure map keys whenever they differ from the cached linear-memory header/shadow.\n- `MAJOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:95` | Semantic fidelity (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:533-545, 564-580, 709-719`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:581-584`): Plan §2.3 `:call` (`Host fn`) only specifies the non-blocking result transition and omits the `run-call-effect` blocking contract and `:park-entry-fns` wiring. | Specify in §2.3 (`:call` -> `Host fn`) that when a host function returns a `module/effect?` value after `engine/check-callee-effect!`, the adapter builds `payload = (payload-of vm inst)` (which sets `:resume-mode :return-result` and `:dest nil` when `tail?` is true, else `:write-result` and `:dest rd`), passes `{:park-entry-fns (park-entry-fns payload)}` (covering `:stream/put`, `:stream/next`, and `:module/require`) to `engine/handle-effect`, advances `:pc` to `pc + 1` on the blocked state when `blocked?` is true, and when `blocked?` is false either runs `(return-transition state value)` (if `tail?`) or writes `value` to `rd` at `pc + 1` on `state`.\n- `MINOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:95, 151` | Continuation invocation check order (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:676, 729-733`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:691-708`): `engine/operator-kind` verifies continuation ownership (`:foreign-continuation`) before `engine/continuation-argument` checks exact 1-argument arity (`:continuation-arity`). Plan §3.2 line 151 and earlier drafts reversed or grouped these checks without fixing the order. | State explicitly in §2.3 and §3.2 that `:call` on a continuation checks ownership via `engine/operator-kind` *before* checking arity via `engine/continuation-argument`.\n- `MINOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:98-99` | Halted state preservation (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:432, 745-747`, `test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc:292-295`): `:halt` and empty-`K` `:return` leave `:pc` at the `:halt`/`:return` instruction pc (not `pc + 1`) and retain the halting body's `:registers` and `:frames` on the halted VM. | Clarify in §2.3 (`:return` and `:halt`) that halting leaves `:pc` at the halting instruction pc and preserves the active body's `:registers` and `:frames` on the halted VM state.\n- `MINOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:175, 233` | Wait-entry oracle scope & custody gates (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc:372-379`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2162-2189, 2664-2715`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc:209-218`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:601-636`): `effects/wait-entry-defect` only accepts the four R2 stream/FFI shapes and returns `{:rule :wait-shape}` for `:link-request`, `:link-response`, `:install`, and gated `:observe` wait entries; also `:yin.k/gate` custody-gate behavior across stream effects, FFI `put-request`, and `check-wait-set` is not listed in W3. | Scope `effects/wait-entry-defect` in §4.2 to stream (`:put`/`:next`) and FFI (`:call-id`/`:request-sent`) wait entries (using `effects/continuation-defect` + link-wait shape checks for module require waits), and include `:yin.k/gate` custody-gate parity cases in W3.\n- `MINOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:193-198, 239` | Module attachment details (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:139, 192-227`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc:84-120`): When caching component-relative wasm modules with an instance `base` offset, `effects/continuation-payload` still requires the relocated instruction tuple from the combined `(:segment vm)` at absolute `(:pc vm)`; and `create-vm` with an empty image seeds `:images` with `[[empty-R 0 0]]` while `attach-image` leaves an empty-base VM's `:halted? true` and `:registers []` unchanged. | Specify in §5 that component instances add `base` to all exported pcs (`pc`, `site-pc`, `return-pc`, `:body-pc`), that `payload-of` always reads `inst` from the relocated combined `:segment`, and that `create-vm` / `attach-image` preserve the `[empty-R 0 0]` initial offset row and empty-base `:halted?`/`:registers` state.\n\n### Properties Passing Review\n\n1. **Core Wasm Execution Model (§1.1, §2.1, §2.2)**: i32 `ValueRef` locals with task-owned value arenas, body-indexed wasm functions with `br_table` intra-body dispatch, and a host trampoline keeping zero suspended guest frames on the native wasm stack.\n2. **Contract & Identity Preservation (§Decision, §2.3, §5)**: Exact preservation of register contract `\"r2\"` (version 4), 23 opcodes, `L`/`T` register banking, 6 in-band `live` operands, BLAKE3 `R` checksums, and `A` as the sole code identity with wasm modules treated strictly as disposable local caches.\n3. **Continuation Model & Multi-Shot Semantics (§3.1–§3.3)**: Exact `effects/continuation-payload` / return-frame shapes, multi-shot reified continuation invocation without native stack unwinding, and explicit separation of same-task `register-restore` image-membership checks from cross-task layout/transport gates.\n4. **FFI Two-Step & Scheduler Ordering (§4.1–§4.3)**: `ffi/require-call-pair!` before id minting or parking, correlated `[caller-token local-id]` call ids, `ok` vs `full` (`:request-sent`) two-step transition without duplicate appends, stale-wake key stripping via `ffi/response-wait-entry`, and `engine/run-loop` / `halted-with-empty-queue?` ordering.\n5. **Append-Only Module Growth & `IModuleKernel` Seam (§5)**: Relocation of `:pc`-kind operands, `[R offset length]` offset-table growth, preservation of in-flight absolute pcs across `attach-image`, isolated `spawn-module` state, and `reset` vs `load-image` code-space retention.\n6. **Slice Structure & Corpus Grounding (§6)**: Falsifiable W0–W6 gates properly accounting for open expressions and parked-id fixtures in `test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc` and full state/trace comparisons beyond B0 value normalization in `test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc`.\n7. **Design-vs-Implementation Discrepancy Analysis (§Decision)**: Accurate identification of stale return-frame code-space prose in `yin.vm.debruijn.register.md` §5.2, `:resource-updates` vs `:store-updates` in `yin.vm.engine.md`, and `vm/machine-data?` / `engine/encoder` continuation refusal behavior in current code.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
